<file path="README.md">
# QuantumSynth Ultimate — Neural Edition

A tiny Go backend plus a WebGL/Three.js audio visualizer frontend. It captures system audio, mic, or a demo oscillator, then drives a shader scene with bass/mid/high bands. Includes a quick control panel, a share panel with QR, a simple 16-step sequencer, and a keep-alive WebSocket.

## Features
- Shader-based visualizer driven by bass/mid/high bands, with tint presets and “flavor” presets (hotkeys 1–5).
- Audio input modes: System (screen-audio), Mic, or built-in Osc demo.
- Overlay bars spectrum and on-canvas status messages.
- Control panel: smoothing, FFT size, sensitivity, theme, fullscreen.
- Share panel: copy current URL and pop-up QR code.
- Simple 16-step sequencer (square-wave bleeps) with BPM control.
- Go server: `/api/health`, `/api/version`, `/ws` with ping keep-alive, CORS, optional security headers, and SPA static serving.

## Quick start

### Requirements
- Node 18+
- Go 1.21+

### 1) Backend
```bash
go run .
# listens on :8080 by default
2) Frontend (dev)
bash
Copy code
cd frontend
npm i
# tell the frontend where the backend is
VITE_BACKEND_BASE=http://localhost:8080 npm run dev
# Vite on :5173
Open http://localhost:5173 and:

Click System to capture system audio. On Chrome, pick “Entire screen” and tick “Share audio”.

Or Mic for microphone input, or Demo for the oscillator.

3) Production build
bash
Copy code
cd frontend && npm run build
cd ..
# serve ./frontend/dist (default). Or override STATIC_DIR.
STATIC_DIR=./frontend/dist PORT=8080 ENABLE_SECURITY_HEADERS=1 go run .
Controls
Hotkeys: 1..5 switch visual “flavor” presets.

Panel (top-right):

System / Mic / Demo input

Smoothing (analyser smoothing)

FFT size (512…8192)

Sensitivity (visual gain)

Theme (Purple, Neon, Sunset, Lush, Candy)

Fullscreen

Share panel (bottom-right):

Copy link

Show QR

Sequencer (bottom-left):

16 toggles + BPM slider

Play/Stop buttons

API and sockets
GET /api/health — returns { status, time }

GET /api/version — returns { version, buildTime }

WS /ws — upgraded connection; server pings on a schedule for keep-alive.

Configuration (env)
Var	Default	Notes
PORT	8080	Listen port
STATIC_DIR	./frontend/dist	Directory for static SPA build
ALLOWED_ORIGINS	empty	CSV of allowed Origin values for WS & CORS. Empty allows all.
ENABLE_SECURITY_HEADERS	0	Set 1 to add CSP, frame, and permissions headers
Frontend VITE_BACKEND_BASE	none	Set in dev so the browser connects to the Go server for /ws and /api

Troubleshooting
System audio says no track: Use HTTPS or localhost, pick “Entire screen”, and tick “Share audio”. Some sites/app windows won’t forward audio.

WS not connected: In dev, set VITE_BACKEND_BASE to your Go server origin. In prod, serve the built SPA from the Go server so origins match.

CORS/Origins: For locked-down deployments, set ALLOWED_ORIGINS to the exact site origins.

Tech
Frontend: Vite, TypeScript, Three.js, WebAudio, QRCode

Backend: Go, gorilla/mux, gorilla/websocket, gorilla/handlers (CORS)

License
MIT.
